  "notes": "Home-automation routine editor (Zapier-like linear step builder) with strong 'dry run against recorded history' concept: day tabs re-simulate the routine, painting each step card with run status pills (✓ 8:15 PM, Stopped, Not reached) and greying unreached steps. Step cards carry a colour-coded left accent bar and kicker per type (trigger indigo, condition amber, action teal, flow purple). Branch step expands into side-by-side 'IF TRUE' (tinted purple, 'taken on Tue, Nov 10') and 'OTHERWISE' (greyed) lanes. Expressions use a small DSL with syntax colouring; the inspector offers clickable variable tokens (now(), ada.swim_days...) that insert into the expression and shows per-clause live evaluation plus a row of time-slot true/false cells across the evening. Warm off-white page (#f4f3ef) with deep navy top bar and yellow 'Enable routine' CTA. Swimlane chart shows family member presence bars with letter avatars."
}
